<title>SWEDEN: Kosta Boda trade to resume - Stockholm bourse.</title>
<headline>Kosta Boda trade to resume - Stockholm bourse.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stockholm bourse said trade in prestige glass company Orrefors Kosta Boda would resume at 1520 GMT on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Earlier, a consortium of Swedish investment group Proventus AB, Denmark's Royal Copenhagen and Scandinavian Equity Partners Ltd -- a Swedish/American investment company -- made a takeover bid for Kosta Boda.</p>
<p>The consortium said in a statement that it was bidding 155 crowns per share and the company's main shareholder Investor AB had already agreed to sell its 23.1 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
